  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "Ernie 4.5 MoE looked up its optional expert-score correction tensor under `moe_statics.e_score_correction_bias`, but `BlockSparseMLP.get_tensors` exported it under `gate.e_score_correction_bias`. A standalone checkpoint containing only the exported spelling could not restore the tensor with the old lookup.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2",
          "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9",
          "call_23d632a4bcb54298b74670b7778768b6"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The one-line change makes Ernie's lookup agree with the shared module's export name and constructor default. This supports interpreting the fix as alignment with ExLlamaV3's serialized format, not a correction to Baidu's checkpoint spelling: the sampled Baidu PT headers use the old name.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2",
          "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9",
          "call_7414502a02884096ad6815da0e6e9262",
          "call_ce92b4dab9c4416eace5c70920fac170"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Turboderp's commit message says the tensor is \u201cnot used.\u201d That is true of Ernie's routing calculation, not of loading or export. Ernie leaves `router_type` at `std`: `routing_std` selects top-k gate logits and applies softmax to the selected logits without consulting the correction tensor. The unselected `routing_ds3` and `routing_dots` helpers do consume it. Neither the router selection nor the gate projection changes.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2",
          "call_b84935913eef479a9bfa613c521181ba",
          "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "A checkpoint that already contains the `gate` spelling can now restore the correction tensor. A source containing only the `moe_statics` spelling instead yields `None` and does not re-export that tensor. Supporting both formats would require a fallback or explicit remapping; this patch adds neither. The tensor's presence does not change expert selection or weights on the inspected standard routing path.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2",
          "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9",
          "call_23d632a4bcb54298b74670b7778768b6"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
