    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "ernie-moe-bias-key",
        "title": "Read the correction tensor under the name ExLlamaV3 exports",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "`Ernie4_5MoEModel.__init__` supplies the suffix only to `BlockSparseMLP`, not to the dense-prefix `GatedMLP`. The shared loader appends the suffix to `model.layers.<idx>.mlp` and makes one optional exact-key lookup. A missing key returns `None`, not an exception or a lookup under the other spelling. The correction tensor is separate from the unchanged router matrix `gate.weight` and from Linear's optional `gate.bias`.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2",
              "call_b84935913eef479a9bfa613c521181ba",
              "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9",
              "call_23d632a4bcb54298b74670b7778768b6",
              "call_6437dcd491ac4de2a46ffd890f6391e3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The four pinned baidu 21B configs\u2014`ERNIE-4.5-21B-A3B-Base-PT`, `ERNIE-4.5-21B-A3B-Base-Paddle`, `ERNIE-4.5-21B-A3B-PT`, and `ERNIE-4.5-21B-A3B-Paddle`\u2014each map to this architecture with hidden size 2560, 28 layers, one dense-prefix layer, 64 routed experts, six selected per token, expert width 1536 and two shared experts. All supply the one-layer interval and omit `head_dim` and `moe_gate_act`; the builder derives head width from the 20 query heads and the sparse module still defaults to `std`. None of these config values supplies the checkpoint key.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c2c3ca4b178d49cf94ac330f0c7098c6",
              "call_886f29ad015a47958a0914f901298463",
              "call_d7cda8687dd744acba655c9d491b62d0",
              "call_31894b9e47464d6c803a803f67c0fa08",
              "call_b84935913eef479a9bfa613c521181ba",
              "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The seven pinned baidu 300B configs\u2014`ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-Base-PT`, `ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-Base-Paddle`, `ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-PT`, `ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-Paddle`, `ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-2Bits-Paddle`, `ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-FP8-Paddle`, and `ERNIE-4.5-300B-A47B-W4A8C8-TP4-Paddle`\u2014each map to hidden size 8192, 54 layers, three dense-prefix layers, 64 routed experts, eight selected per token and expert width 3584. Each supplies interval one, omits `head_dim` and uses the derived width from 64 query heads, omits the shared-expert count and defaults it to zero, and omits `moe_gate_act`. The quantized variants' format declarations do not change the builder's correction-name lookup or router selection.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5e01d05e6cf845a8a93a1c3404e20630",
              "call_41edf21710d8480b9320aec640022713",
              "call_277827eb7c2c455686a805b25134c3f2",
              "call_b9c11542aa8d45d7880286ec384c26de",
              "call_ed776cb20d72432dbf43c8146081bad5",
              "call_4f3f451b22c042de9b3a309839c0b2cf",
              "call_7aa3fd8643c8434988dfde568f5a475b",
              "call_b84935913eef479a9bfa613c521181ba",
              "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The 21B Base-PT and PT header samples list `model.layers.1.mlp.moe_statics.e_score_correction_bias` as BF16 `[1,64]`; the 300B Base-PT and PT samples list `model.layers.3.mlp.moe_statics.e_score_correction_bias` as F32 `[1,64]`. That is one stored value per routed expert, with no shape validation added by the patch. These samples list `gate.weight` at `[64,2560]` or `[64,8192]` but do not list the newly requested `gate.e_score_correction_bias` beside it. The new correction lookup never requests the stored `moe_statics` name and will take the optional-miss path if the new name is absent from the file map.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_7414502a02884096ad6815da0e6e9262",
              "call_61e17dada507487e84d583eb12ee65b9",
              "call_ce92b4dab9c4416eace5c70920fac170",
              "call_8ff351828b424827917113d5c3698571",
              "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2",
              "call_23d632a4bcb54298b74670b7778768b6"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Matching config dimensions does not imply Paddle weight compatibility. The 21B Base-Paddle sample stores `ernie.layers.15.mlp.moe_statics.e_score_correction_bias` at `[1,64]`, `gate.weight` and a `gate.weight_1` at `[2560,64]`, and fused `up_gate_proj.weight` at `[2560,3072]` for a routed expert. The builder requests none of those exact names. The 300B Base-Paddle sample likewise uses an `ernie` prefix and fused `up_gate_proj`; the 2Bits, FP8 and W4A8C8-TP4 samples contain `quant_weight` names rather than the requested separate projections. Changing the correction suffix adds no translation for those layouts.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9591d0d5aa6b4db3ab8dd6b72c7228a1",
              "call_6c4e285dc11b4e38b37cb177013bb6c3",
              "call_dc802b08ffe64da78d272bfa342e6858",
              "call_037a98418e934602aebc0c09335b6eb3",
              "call_ed45487ff78949baacef18a698097b3b",
              "call_b84935913eef479a9bfa613c521181ba",
              "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The direct sparse load is reached by recursive `Module.load` because `TransformerBlock` registers its MLP. Conversion also loads the block, iterates its registered modules for `get_tensors`, saves the result, and reloads with those tensors as an overlay. The compiler copies the resulting names by prefix into output shards. The new name therefore fixes agreement with an already-exported tensor, but changing the input name can also prevent that tensor from entering a fresh export in the first place.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_f8d1694280154f8d99df0fbae9ac79e7",
              "call_638680646e5547bc983af9c973385bfb",
              "call_968a115aa8944d0eadbae8f11a1a6fc5",
              "call_ae89f24a3d7d408aaead880bdbc3187f",
              "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9",
              "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library transcription found that an old-name-only source returns the modeled bias before the change and `None` after it; a standalone gate-name-only export gives the opposite result. It also showed that the old-name lookup can still hit the original files beneath an export overlay. Integer arithmetic gave head width 128 for both families, 27 versus 51 sparse layers, and shared width 3072 versus no shared branch. No tensor operations ran.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b3b2de9870ab4b03b7ef936be3640826"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The ancestor's fused-path observations are carried over: the diff changes only the bias suffix, leaving all-expert dispatch, selected-expert-sized buffers and the workspace-backed return unchanged. The original ChatML-formatting observation is separate and no longer describes the MoE parent: its formatter already emits the begin-of-sentence marker and `User:`/`Assistant:` labels.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b5c5dd9b7dee4fc6b7be8b59b36eaba2",
              "call_ef5f05a7f9ed45e0b73d72837a1e7fc9",
              "call_b84935913eef479a9bfa613c521181ba"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
